# Implementation Plan: FastAPI To-Do Backend

## Goal Description
Create a Python backend using FastAPI, Uvicorn, and SQLite for the To-Do application. Provides a RESTful API to manage to-do items.

## Proposed Changes
### Backend Structure
- Create a new directory `backend` parallel to `frontend`.
- Set up a Python virtual environment.

### Database Content
#### [NEW] backend/database.py
- SQLAlchemy configuration for SQLite database `todos.db`.

#### [NEW] backend/models.py
- SQLAlchemy `Todo` model (id, title, description, completed).

#### [NEW] backend/schemas.py
- Pydantic models for request/response validation (`TodoCreate`, `TodoResponse`, `TodoUpdate`).

#### [NEW] backend/main.py
- FastAPI application instance.
- CRUD endpoints:
  - `GET /todos/`: List all to-dos.
  - `POST /todos/`: Create a new to-do.
  - `GET /todos/{todo_id}`: Get a specific to-do.
  - `PUT /todos/{todo_id}`: Update a to-do.
  - `DELETE /todos/{todo_id}`: Delete a to-do.

## Verification Plan
### Automated Tests
- Run the FastAPI application using `uvicorn main:app --reload`.
- Test the endpoints using FastAPI's built-in Swagger UI at `http://localhost:8000/docs`.
